Now we're established:
Client
  │
  │ TCP connection
  ▼
LB
Client sends:
GET /orders/123
TCP breaks application data into segments as needed.
The receiving side gets an ordered byte stream.
The application calls:
read()
and obtains available bytes.
Again:
TCP:
"Here are bytes."

HTTP:
"These bytes represent GET /orders/123."
